Python: `except A, B:` and `except A, B, C:` (PEP 758, Python 3.14) are now
parsed as an unparenthesized tuple of exception types, like `except (A, B):`,
instead of being read as the Python 2 `except A as B:` form (or, for three or
more types, failing to parse). The Python 2 reading is still used when scanning
with `python2` as the language.
